; `quotient` by a zero divisor is fatal on both substrates for every operand
; representation. R7RS 6.2.6 makes a zero n2 an error for the whole
; integer-division trio, and the alternative here was not a NaN but a
; plausible integer: native truncated +inf.0 and clamped the FPToSI to the
; int64 range, so (quotient 5.0 0.0) answered 9223372036854774784.
(display (quotient 5.0 0.0))
(display "MUST-NOT-PRINT")
